|YKOInvasions are announced by Darkwind's Invasion Plan and Protection
Siren, usually called DIPPS. Invaders can roam Darkwind City,
attack players and residents, and damage shops until defenders win or the
invasion succeeds. DIPPS announces the all-clear when it is safe.

New and low-level characters should leave the city when an invasion begins.
Do not assume the Center of Town, a shop, or an ordinary travel route is safe.
Services may remain unavailable while damaged locations are repaired.

Bosses are named encounters stronger and more rewarding than ordinary
monsters. Many show a tier from T1 through T5; a higher tier usually means
more health, pressure, mechanics, and reward expectations. Treat the tier as
a clue, not a promise that your build is ready.

Other long-term challenges include the Eternal Dungeon, the arena,
achievements and achievement titles, daily rewards, and unique equipment.
|YKBachievements|YKO reviews your progress, |YKBleaderboard|YKO shows the
achievement leaders, |YKBdaily|YKO checks the shared daily reward, and
|YKBuniques|YKO explains one-copy items.

At level 100, level gives way to renown as HERO, ADV, or VILN according to
your deeds. Level 150 earns LEGEND status and another multichar slot. At
level 250, remort trades your level for permanent boon points and begins the
climb again. Specialization and the metaphysician path add further veteran
progression.

Events are easier and safer with other players. Read the event's help before
joining, watch public announcements, and ask whether a party is forming.|000

